WEBVTT

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.950
There's nobody here.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:17.000
This place is usually
teeming with adventurers...

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.040
Perhaps they all evacuated because
of a monster attack or something?

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.460
I doubt such a coward
would make it this far.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.460
I heard from an older adventurer once...

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:33.640
A long time ago, a hero and his partner
set out to rescue the hero's lover

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.140
from a dragon.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.890
The hero managed to beat the dragon,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.810
but the partner, a mage,
stabbed him in the back.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.900
The hero was imprisoned,
wasn't able to see his lover,

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:51.490
and died in grief, wallowing in despair.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:57.040
Since that day, the ghost of
the hero haunts this dungeon...

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.960
So the ghost did this?

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.120
That's impossible.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.840
What's that?!

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:11.760
Ghosts?!

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.560
No. Judging from their gear,
they're the adventurers that stayed here.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:23.810
Seriously?!

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.440
Let go, dammit!

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:31.780
Eldman!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.580
Oh no! He joined them!

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.120
What was that?

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:50.670
I don't know. But that's probably
what happened to the people here.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.800
We're going after them,
right, Mr. Ninomiya?

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.970
Mr. Ninomiya?

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.310
Episode 9: The Silent Fortress

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.390
Is that...

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.730
Ninomiya's underwear?

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:08.900
Wait, so he's running around buck naked?!

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.360
I smell Kinji.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.610
Huh? You can tell, Rim?

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.280
Yeah, this way.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.580
Here.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:21.120
Here? The wall?

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:25.960
A hidden passage?!

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.340
No, it's a staircase
hidden by illusion magic.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.180
So Ninomiya left
his underwear there as a hint.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.430
There's no doubt
Mr. Ninomiya is down there.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.520
Is that...

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.240
Eldman!

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.990
What are they doing?

00:02:56.990 --> 00:03:01.200
An illegal potion factory?

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.700
I can't take this anymore!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.460
Dammit! He's coming this way!

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.130
They'll bite us!

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:13.090
No, they're...

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:17.220
If you leave, we can't meet our quotas.

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:20.890
If you're going to leave,
at least find a replacement.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.310
What are they doing?

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:25.930
That's an incantation.
Magic based on words.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:33.400
It seems like listening to their
whispers makes you join them.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.360
So it's not an infection after all.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.070
And the flow of magic
is coming from... There.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.620
It's written in some kind of
special language I can't read,

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:41.990
"Three Vows of the Good Employee"

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:48.210
but it seems to be auto-managing
the curse put on the adventurers.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:46.000
"1. Find your own work and
tackle it like your life depends on it!"

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.000
"2. Don't hesitate to affect your
surroundings! Good results await!"

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:52.960
So if we destroy it,
would that bring everyone back?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.040
"3. If you set a goal,
accomplish it, even if it kills you!"

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.210
Probably.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:58.800
But how do we get to it
through all of them?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.890
Hmm... In that case...

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.940
Wh-Why...

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.650
I can't believe this worked...

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.320
The magic itself should be simple,

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:23.030
so we can just blend in and work,
and try to find an opening.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.950
If you miss the mixture ratio by
even one drop, no break for you.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.330
Three drops of the blue ingredient,
three drops of the green...

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:37.340
Ugh, repeating the same
work over and over... This is tough.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:40.880
There's no opening to leave our station.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.640
You there!

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.470
Y-Yes?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:50.100
This is terrible! Re-do them all!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.850
I'm going to the restroom!

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.270
No. You'll delay everyone's work.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.860
But I have to!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:01.360
If you have to, use this bottle.

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.200
Don't be stupid!

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:08.250
Idiot! That's going to...

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:16.880
We're surrounded!

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.170
There's nothing to do now
but force our way through!

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.720
Why do you sound so excited?!

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.640
Eldman!

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:30.180
How are we supposed to deal
with such a huge horde of zombies?!

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.140
I'll hold them off!

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.310
I want to show off for a change!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.110
Fine.

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:40.150
Ranga, you're the quickest one here.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:42.820
Go and break that weird thing!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.860
Okay!

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.570
--Let's go!
--Yes.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.180
Take this!

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:08.430
Now!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.020
Come!

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.140
Yes!

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.780
I did it!

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.450
What is this place?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.370
What are we...

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.790
O-Oh, I'm so tired...

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.920
Looks like the magic
was successfully dispelled.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.140
Why does my left side hurt so much...?

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.970
Where's Ninomiya?

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.060
There's nobody left here.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.310
Are there other places like this?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.610
Kinji's scent is coming from here.

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.030
Rim...

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:07.320
What's your relationship with Ninomiya?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.160
Before, he was food.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.290
F-Food?!

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.670
I thought he might taste funny.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:20.920
But now, it is fun to be with him.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.500
I see.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.760
I came here to teach my ancestor a lesson,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:30.930
but at the end of the day, I really enjoy
hanging out with Ninomiya and the others.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.850
Fun... Huh...

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:43.780
Yes, Mr. Ninomiya can be a ridiculously
selfish miser, but being with him...

00:07:43.780 --> 00:07:45.400
Is Mr. Ninomiya in here?

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.030
For sure.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.870
Mr. Ninomiya, I will save you
because I have to!

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:57.830
Mr. Ninomiya!

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.880
Come on! Put more of your grudge into it!

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:03.710
I'm sorry!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.510
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.840
I'm sorry!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.930
Um... Mr. Ninomiya?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.850
Oh, you came?

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:18.020
What do you mean "you came"?
We thought you were abducted!

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:21.650
Well, yeah. I was abducted.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.730
When the zombies attacked you,
I got dragged into the wall...

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:29.400
...by this one!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.570
Ouch!

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.950
Who is this?

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:37.040
It's the "mage" from the story.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.540
Not the hero who was tricked by the mage?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:45.460
So why is the mage here...?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:48.550
Well, that's a long story...

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.550
Keep it short!

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:59.520
Several hundred years ago, I worked
with a swordsman who was called a hero.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:04.310
He was such an insufferably selfish man.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:08.490
He went off and accepted a
contract to save a girl from a dragon

00:09:08.490 --> 00:09:10.490
without even asking.

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:14.070
I beat the dragon while
almost getting myself killed.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:19.120
But he just watched
and afterwards, said...

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.830
I totally hit it off with the girl!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.920
I think I'll go ahead and call off our
partnership and work with her instead!

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:30.920
After hearing those words of betrayal
from my long-time partner,

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:36.100
I used a barrier spell
to lock him in this dungeon.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:39.220
So that's where
this connects to the story.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:43.060
But he forcefully broke the barrier,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:47.270
and so I was labeled the traitor instead.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:50.990
After losing my social status,

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:55.990
I was forced to work in this
dungeon under terrible conditions.

00:09:55.990 --> 00:10:00.080
I cursed the whole world
as I died from overwork.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:07.170
But you remained as a vengeful spirit
and gained this new form.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:12.470
Now that I've made a comeback, I thought
I should make humans suffer like I did.

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:17.470
I see. So how does that connect
to you abducting Ninomiya?

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:22.480
The atmosphere this person has about him
is similar to the hero I mentioned.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.060
I got the urge to brainwash him
with my own hands.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:30.480
I won't be brainwashed by
a weak-willed loser like you!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.240
It must have been tough for you, too.

00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:39.740
Actually, Mr. Ninomiya lectured some
sense into me, and I've made a decision.

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:41.200
Huh?

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:53.670
I will release myself
onto the surface world!

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.090
Then...

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.720
I will make the whole world
suffer through the experience

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:02.470
of working until you drop from exhaustion!

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:08.610
This is bad!

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.860
But, um...

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:16.070
Corporate drones already exist
pretty widely in this world, right?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:21.240
Don't give it away so quickly...

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.620
Um... What does that mean?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.670
Put simply...

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.750
This whole world is already
full of corporate drones

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:35.470
and doesn't need your help forcing workers
to work until they drop from exhaustion!

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:41.350
I... I had no idea...

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:47.020
Even without my help, the world is headed
in a stupid direction all by itself...

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:48.850
Yes.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:54.610
In that case... I have no more regrets.

00:11:54.610 --> 00:12:01.620
I'm sorry I caused trouble.
And Mr. Ninomiya...

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.620
The last few moments I spent with you...

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.750
I've enjoyed very much.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:10.710
Thank you.

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.760
That's settled!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.430
What an unsettling story.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:27.520
What?

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.350
Nothing!

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:33.190
I missed you, Ninomiya!

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:34.690
Kinji!

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:37.400
--Oh, Ninomiya!
--So hungry!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.780
Get off! You're heavy!

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.830
At any rate...

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:48.540
...this is turning out to be
a well-balanced party.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.250
Oh, no, no...

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.750
Sales for this week are terrible...

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:58.050
Headquarters will bite my head off again!

00:12:58.050 --> 00:13:05.060
This is all because that vengeful spirit
mage messed around in the fortress!

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:11.020
Now the customers are scared and
won't even come close to this place!

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:15.900
Maybe I'm just not
cut out to run a business...?

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.990
Hey, manager!

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:21.450
Y-Yes, welcome...

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.490
What's wrong with you?!

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.660
Why would you sell such obviously
frayed clothing like this? Look!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.960
Oh no, a complainer...

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:34.750
I'm truly sorry. I'll bring
a replacement right away...

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:39.260
Not a replacement! All I'm asking for is a
show of good faith, you know what I mean?

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.130
N-No, what should I...

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:43.470
A discount! And a tremendous one at that!

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:49.890
But... that item was already sold
to you at a very large discount...

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:54.310
Then make it free since I took
a defective item off your shelf.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:57.070
That's quite unreasonable...

00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:01.070
What?! After all this good faith
from my side, that's what you--

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.740
Hey! Mr. Ninomiya!

00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:03.610
Ouch...

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.990
Your complaints are absurd!
You're making a scene!

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.450
We're sorry, manager.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:08.620
N-No, I...

00:14:08.620 --> 00:14:10.700
Don't try to end this on your own!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:16.000
We're about to dive into danger,
yet we have no money and no equipment.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.880
You want to play the good guy
and die as a result?

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.880
Well, that's...

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:26.300
Hey. You're just a hired manager that's
getting exploited by Raiza'ha, right?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.140
Huh?

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:32.350
Come on. Just say there was
a defective item or something.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:37.440
It's not like this shop's name has
any personal value for you, right?

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:38.570
That's not right.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:39.480
Hmm?

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:46.660
It might look rather dejected right now,
but my father left me this shop.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:54.080
After Raiza'ha bought up the rights to
this shop and imposed those tough quotas,

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:58.040
sure, things got really tough! But!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.920
I will one day buy back this shop!

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:04.260
This shop is what I live for!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.050
I like that sort of backbone.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:12.770
Goals and aspirations
should always be personal.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:18.360
I hate those who get mixed up and
are content with what they're given.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.940
You are correct.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:24.780
As always, the friend/foe distinction
is quite extreme with him...

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:30.240
Normally, I, Kinji Ninomiya, rarely
spend time taking care of others,

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.040
but this time, it's special.

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:33.120
Huh?

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.960
I will flood this shop with customers!

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:43.380
In return, if I succeed, you will
sell me the best gear in this shop

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.050
at a huge employee discount!

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:48.760
Let's enjoy this rebellion together.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:16:02.650
For starters, Cindy, what's the
biggest selling point for this shop?

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:05.320
Hmm... There's nothing...

00:16:05.320 --> 00:16:09.740
Anything! Leftover inventory, perhaps.

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:11.990
In that case...

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:14.620
That looks way too familiar.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:19.540
These are the potions that the ghost mage
forced everyone to make.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.250
The company forced me to buy them all up.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:24.960
There's a huge number of them, for sure.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:30.760
But they're not high quality at all,
so we'd have to sell at a huge loss...

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.390
No...

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.770
If it has no strengths,
we can just make some.

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:41.690
These ones are strong!

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:42.940
Watch out!

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:50.740
Are you all right?

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.320
Who are you?!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:57.700
Just a passing adventurer.
Leave this to us and stand back.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.790
But before we continue...

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.000
I'm getting pumped up!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.010
Dead Cow, for in-combat
nutritional supplementation!

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:14.930
So strong!

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:18.220
What was that drink? A potion?!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.310
That was Dead Cow!

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:19.930
Huh?

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:20.810
Who are you?!

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:26.110
1,000 milligrams of concentrated mana,
a new potion for the fighting adventurer!

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:28.070
That's Dead Cow!

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.030
D-Dead Cow!

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.820
Hello.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:37.160
Dead Cow, when you want
to go that extra step further!

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.500
We're handing them out
for free, limited offer.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:40.410
Free?!

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.870
Then I'll take it!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.960
Sure! Here you go!

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:51.630
They're being sold on the third floor
in Cindy's shop in the fort.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:55.550
Please consider purchasing
some if you like it!

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.890
Please...

00:17:56.970 --> 00:18:01.890
Watch the
 circuit breaker
when using
microwave!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.680
Oh, I'm so tired from
working the night shift!

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:01.850
I don't think I can
conquer the world today.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.900
Then it's time for this! Dead Cow!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:03.970
Dead Cow

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:03.970
Dead Cow

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.480
Wow! 300 million times more energy!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:10.780
I'm all topped up!

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:13.490
Now I can fight 168 hours straight!

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:16.200
I've regrown my wings and adult teeth!

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.330
I can shoot lasers from my belly button!

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.250
My dead grandma came back to life!

00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:21.540
Yay!

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.120
30,000 kilometers per bottle! Dead Cow!

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:26.840
Available now at Cindy's Shop!

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:36.720
Yes! Thank you!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.470
So many customers...

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:43.100
Dead Cow... How did you come up with this?

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:49.230
Image is key. You have to
stimulate their self-satisfaction.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.110
I see...

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:54.650
Plus, I've made it slightly addictive.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:19:00.120
It's the perfect merchandise;
one sip and you're hooked.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.120
Huh...

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:04.080
Wait, addictive?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:06.210
Addiction? That's bad!

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.290
Quiet!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:12.960
It's not strong, just slightly more
addictive than coffee. There's no problem.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:18.010
Look, Cindy. See how happy
they look buying this product?

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.060
This is what you wanted to see, isn't it?

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.390
It is...

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:27.020
These customers are gods,
helping us make our business boom.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:33.610
Customers are gods...
I've never seen it that way before.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:36.820
But yeah, that sounds right.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.070
That said...

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:41.240
I am superior to any god!

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:55.130
Effective immediately, you are
prohibited from selling Dead Cow!

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.050
Huh?

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:58.840
Wh-Why?!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:01.970
We've discovered hypnotic effects
far exceeding the limits set by

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.680
our corporate headquarters.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:10.730
I guess using confusion grass as
a finishing touch for quicker sales

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:11.980
might have been a step too far...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:17.700
The potion that Dead Cow is based
on was made by employees who were

00:20:17.700 --> 00:20:20.450
under the influence of a ghost mage!

00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:23.490
Maybe some remnants of the
ghost's magic power got mixed in!

00:20:23.490 --> 00:20:24.330
Huh?

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.000
What a bunch of nonsense...

00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:30.880
It was not intentional! All we wanted
to do was to minimize company losses!

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:33.550
Wow! Such a direct lie!

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:36.670
That doesn't change the fact that the
product violates company standards.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:39.300
You will explain yourself in headquarters.

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.970
I guess there's no way around this!

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:45.390
Hey, Cindy! Looks like
that's all the help we can give.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:46.600
Huh?

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:52.770
We actually have an
important mission to fulfill!

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:55.610
I'll leave you in charge of the rest!

00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:57.690
He's trying to make a run for it!

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:59.070
B-But...

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:03.910
You can still sell Dead Cow if it doesn't
include ingredients from the ghost mage!

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:06.910
Best of luck in making the shop bigger!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:08.410
Give it your all!

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.290
Yes.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:14.290
You heard me! Get ready, quick!
We're leaving!

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:19.840
Solving the issue and leaving swiftly...

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.800
What a gallant, wonderful man!

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.510
Hey! Mr. Ninomiya!

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.350
Running away so suddenly, that's inhumane!

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.020
You have to help her properly--

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:35.070
She is someone who can grow on her own.

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:41.110
Staying around and taking away her chance
to think on her own is much worse.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.410
I suppose, when I come back,
if she's still moping around,

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:47.410
I can give her a slap on the back.
That much I can do.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:50.870
The ghost mage case, and now this...

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:54.630
He really can't just honestly
help someone, can he?

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:03.260
So this is the fourth floor...

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:08.470
Unbelievable...

00:22:08.470 --> 00:22:11.560
Am I really still in the dungeon?
